Version: 1.0
desc: Speak Volumes Ambisonic Loudspeaker Decoder (SPARTA AmbiDEC port) by chmaha
tags: spatial ambisonics decoder loudspeakers surround hoa 3d allrad
author: chmaha
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  Decodes a 1st to 7th order ambisonic scene to up to 64 loudspeakers. Four decoder designs (sampling SAD,
  mode-matching MMD, energy-preserving EPAD and all-round AllRAD, the default), with separate low and high
  frequency decoders split at an adjustable transition frequency, each with its own max-rE weighting and
  amplitude- or energy-preserving normalisation. The decoding order can be set per frequency band, with
  presets for the Zylia, Eigenmike and DTU microphone arrays. SPARTA's loudspeaker layouts plus REAPER surround
  layouts with a silent LFE channel (L R C LFE ...). An optional binaural monitor renders the virtual loudspeakers
  to headphones with KEMAR head-related transfer functions. ACN or FuMa input with N3D, SN3D or FuMa
  normalisation. Settings are redesigned in the background while the previous decoder keeps playing.
  Ported from SPARTA AmbiDEC and the Spatial_Audio_Framework by Leo McCormack
  https://github.com/leomccormack/SPARTA (GPL-3.0), https://github.com/leomccormack/Spatial_Audio_Framework (ISC)
  afSTFT filterbank by Juha Vilkamo (MIT); convex hull (convhull_3d) by Leo McCormack (MIT), after the quickhull
  by George Papazafeiropoulos (BSD-2); HRIRs: Genelec Aural ID of a KEMAR dummy head, kindly provided by
  Aki Mäkivirta and Jaan Johansson (ISC, see Dependencies/SpeakVolumes/SpeakVolumes-LICENSE.txt)
  JSFX version released under GPL-3.0 license
  Claude generated some of this code
provides:
  Dependencies/SpeakVolumes/hrtf.txt
  Dependencies/SpeakVolumes/SpeakVolumes-LICENSE.txt

